\>", "Subsubsection",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.998490419722283*^9, 3.998490429100876*^9}, {
  3.998490766562622*^9, 
  3.998490770626902*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"bacc06aa-c208-45a2-ad95-\
4ac00179759f"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "Initialize by reading in SamplePort1.m and DistFn1.m from the current \
notebook directory (if files are there) or prompt for full directory name. \
SamplePort1.m sets up the sample portfolio structure: static data for \
instruments and market data. DistFn1.m contains instrument valuation (PV) \
functions, DV01 (bumping) functions, portfolio functions, and risk \
(volatility, variance-covariance, Value-at-Risk) functions. (We also need to \
define some distribution functions because the default functions in ",
 StyleBox["Mathematica",
  FontSlant->"Italic"],
 " do not work for a 2-point mixture of normals.)"
}], "Text",
 CellChangeTimes->{{3.49311721425*^9, 3.4931172481875*^9}, {
  3.498754055578125*^9, 3.49875418975*^9}, {3.998490870337751*^9, 
  3.998490933785602*^9}, {3.99850932303413*^9, 3.998509404962825*^9}, {
  3.9985094623392*^9, 3.998509474435939*^9}, {3.998509542532425*^9, 
  3.9985096436478033`*^9}, {3.999003042876217*^9, 
  3.999003044113913*^9}},ExpressionUUID->"20984f5a-6a01-4eb2-9d1b-\
3123dd7f8a8c"],

